* Behavioural models for the parts on the Totem reference design.
*
* None of these are vendor models. No vendor publishes a SPICE model for an
* ESP32 module, a GNSS receiver or an addressable LED, and what those parts
* do is firmware rather than circuit behaviour. What they present to the
* circuit that surrounds them, though, is a supply current — and that is
* what has to be right for the power design to be checked. So each one is
* modelled as the load it is, at its datasheet figure, and every figure is
* named below.
*
* The parts that are genuinely passive to this circuit — connectors, a
* touch pad, switches, a test point — get the high-resistance stub that is
* the conventional way to keep a netlist solvable without pretending the
* part does something. 1e12 ohms is an open circuit as far as any result
* here is concerned.
*
* Kept in the project rather than referenced from elsewhere on this
* machine, so the simulation runs for anyone who has the repository.

* --------------------------------------------------------------- charger
* TP4056: a linear cell charger. Constant-current to 4.2 V, then constant
* voltage. The current is set by the PROG resistor as I = 1200 / R_PROG,
* so the 1k2 fitted here asks for 1 A. Modelled as a 4.2 V source behind
* the resistance that produces that current limit, which reproduces both
* phases without claiming to model the silicon's loop.
.subckt TP4056 TEMP PROG GND VCC BAT STDBY CHRG CE EPAD
BCHG BAT GND I = (v(CE) > 1.5 && v(VCC) > v(BAT) + 0.2) ? min(1.0, (4.2 - v(BAT)) * 20) : 0
RLEAK BAT GND 1e7
RTEMP TEMP GND 1e12
RSTBY STDBY GND 1e12
RCHRG CHRG GND 1e12
REPAD EPAD GND 1e12
.ends TP4056

* ------------------------------------------------------------- regulator
* AP2127K-3.3, or whatever the SOT-23-5 marked ACH turns out to be: a
* 3.3 V LDO. Output follows the input down once the drop across the pass
* element exceeds the headroom, which is the behaviour the rail has to be
* checked against at the bottom of the discharge. Rpass 0.2 ohm is a
* competent 500 mA part, 100 mV of dropout at full load.
.subckt LDO_3V3 VIN GND EN NC VOUT
BOUT VOUT GND V = (v(EN) > 1.0) ? min(3.3, v(VIN) - 0.2 * abs(i(VSENSE))) : 0
VSENSE VOUT VOUTX 0
RL VOUTX GND 1e9
RNC NC GND 1e12
.ends LDO_3V3

* ------------------------------------------------------------------ MCU
* ESP32-WROOM-32E. Datasheet: 500 mA peak during an RF transmit burst,
* around 95 mA average with the radio active, 3.0 to 3.6 V supply. The
* peak is what the rail must survive; it is a burst with a low duty cycle,
* which is why the pass element's dissipation at that current is transient.
.subckt ESP32 VDD GND
IPEAK VDD GND 500m
.ends ESP32

* ----------------------------------------------------------------- GNSS
* MAX-M10S: about 31 mA while acquiring, less once it has a fix.
.subckt MAXM10S VCC GND
IACQ VCC GND 31m
.ends MAXM10S

* ------------------------------------------------------------------ IMU
* ICM-20948, gyro and accelerometer and magnetometer all running.
.subckt ICM20948 VDD GND REGOUT
IRUN VDD GND 3m
* REGOUT is the part's own internal regulator, brought out only so its
* decoupling capacitor has something to sit on. About 1.8 V.
VREG REGOUT GND 1.8
.ends ICM20948

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- pixels
* One WS2812B stands for a chain. 60 mA is a pixel at full white; the
* current here is the chain's, at the firmware's default brightness of
* 0.6, which is what the cell actually has to deliver.
.subckt WS2812B_RING VDD GND DIN
IRING VDD GND 2.16
.ends WS2812B_RING

.subckt WS2812B_CRYSTAL VDD GND DIN
ICRY VDD GND 252m
.ends WS2812B_CRYSTAL

* ------------------------------------------------------- passive to this
* Connectors, switches, a capacitive pad, a test point. Open circuits.
.subckt STUB2 A B
R1 A B 1e12
.ends STUB2

.subckt STUB1 A
R1 A 0 1e12
.ends STUB1

.subckt STUB3 A B C
R1 A B 1e12
R2 B C 1e12
.ends STUB3

* A p-channel switch passing the cell to the LED rail. Gate low turns it
* on, which is how GPIO 19 drives it.
.subckt PMOS_SW G S D
BSW S D I = (v(G) < v(S) - 1.0) ? (v(S) - v(D)) / 0.05 : (v(S) - v(D)) / 1e9
.ends PMOS_SW

* An indicator LED and its forward drop.
.subckt LED_IND A K
D1 A K DLED
.model DLED D (IS=1e-14 N=2.0 RS=5)
.ends LED_IND

* The microphone, as the bias network sees it: a high impedance.
.subckt MIC_MEMS M P
R1 P M 2e3
.ends MIC_MEMS
